# 🦺 PPE (Helmet & Safety Vest) Detection Dashboard

A Streamlit app that uses YOLOv8 to detect helmets and safety vests from a
live webcam, an uploaded image, or an uploaded video — no model training required.

## Features
- 📷 **Live webcam detection** (real-time, via `streamlit-webrtc`)
- 🖼️ **Upload image** detection with side-by-side original/annotated view
- 🎞️ **Upload video** detection with frame-skipping for speed
- 📊 **Dashboard**: cumulative class counts, compliance rate, time-series chart
- ✅/❌ Compliant vs non-compliant people counter

## Project structure
```
ppe_detection_app/
├── app.py                 # Streamlit UI (4 modes)
├── requirements.txt
├── utils/
│   └── detector.py        # YOLOv8 wrapper + drawing/counting logic
├── models/
│   └── ppe.pt              # <-- put your PPE-trained YOLOv8 weights here
└── sample_data/            # put test images/videos here (optional)
```

## 1. Setup

```bash
cd ppe_detection_app
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## 2. Get PPE detection weights (no training needed)

A stock `yolov8n.pt` only knows COCO classes (person, car, dog, ...) — it does
**not** know "helmet" or "safety vest". You need weights fine-tuned on a PPE
dataset. Easiest options, no training required:

**Option A — Roboflow Universe (recommended, free)**
1. Go to https://universe.roboflow.com and search "PPE detection" or
   "Construction Site Safety" (there are many public pre-trained YOLOv8 models,
   e.g. models trained on the popular "Construction Site Safety Image Dataset"
   with classes: `Hardhat, Mask, NO-Hardhat, NO-Mask, NO-Safety Vest, Person,
   Safety Cone, Safety Vest, machinery, vehicle`).
2. Open a model page → "Deploy" tab → download the YOLOv8 `.pt` weights
   (Roboflow lets you export trained weights directly, or use their hosted
   inference API if you prefer not to download).
3. Rename the file to `ppe.pt` and place it in the `models/` folder.

**Option B — Hugging Face Hub**
Search for community PPE/hard-hat YOLOv8 checkpoints (several exist under
tags like `keremberke/yolov8*-construction-safety` or similar hard-hat
detection repos) and download the `.pt` file into `models/ppe.pt`.

**Option C — Quick test with generic COCO model**
If you just want to confirm the app runs, set the model path in the sidebar
to `yolov8n.pt` (Ultralytics will auto-download it). It will only detect
`person`, not helmets/vests — the app will show a warning banner in this case.

> ⚠️ The class names in `utils/detector.py` (`POSITIVE_CLASSES`,
> `NEGATIVE_CLASSES`, `PERSON_CLASSES`) assume the common
> `Hardhat / NO-Hardhat / Safety Vest / NO-Safety Vest / Person` naming
> scheme. If your chosen model uses different label names (e.g. `helmet`,
> `no-helmet`), just add them to those sets — no code logic changes needed.

## 3. Run the app

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

Then open the URL Streamlit prints (usually http://localhost:8501).

## 4. Usage
- **Live Webcam**: select the mode, click "START", allow camera permission.
- **Upload Image / Video**: drag and drop a file; annotated results and
  counts appear automatically and are logged to the Dashboard.
- **Dashboard**: view cumulative PPE class counts, compliance rate over time,
  and a chart of detections. Click "Clear history" to reset.

## Notes & tips
- Adjust the **confidence threshold** slider in the sidebar to reduce false
  positives/negatives.
- For video mode, increase "Process every Nth frame" to speed up processing
  on longer clips.
- `compliant_people` / `non_compliant_people` are computed heuristically:
  any `NO-Hardhat` / `NO-Safety Vest` (etc.) detection counts as a
  non-compliance flag; remaining detected people are counted as compliant.
  Adjust the logic in `utils/detector.py` -> `PPEDetector.detect()` if your
  use case needs stricter per-person matching (e.g. matching each hardhat box
  to a specific person box via IoU/overlap).

## Troubleshooting
- **Webcam not showing up**: browsers require HTTPS or `localhost` for camera
  access; if deploying remotely, serve over HTTPS.
- **Model not found error**: double check the path typed in the sidebar
  matches where you placed the `.pt` file.
- **Slow inference on CPU**: use a smaller model variant (`yolov8n` size) and/or
  increase frame skipping in video mode.